{
  "about": "Every weapon the engine knows, by generic id. Weapons are data: a `warhead` (its row in the combat module's damage table) and tunable numbers. Distances are sub-tile units (256 per tile), times are ticks. `speed` 0 means an instant hit; otherwise a projectile flies that far each tick and lands within `scatter` of where it was aimed. `splash` is the blast radius: full damage within half of it, half damage within all of it. `hits_air` and `hits_ground` say what it may aim at: aircraft in flight, or anything on the ground (landed aircraft included). A `beam` weapon (its width) hits at once everything along a line `range` long, firer and its own kind excepted; `converts` (ticks) makes a projectile turn enemy vehicles to its side for that long instead of hurting them. Our own numbers, from our own simulation runs. `missile_strike` names the palace missile's hits; its damage by ring is the superpowers module's.",
